      "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss the cotangent complex of a map of sheaves\nof rings on a site. In later sections we specialize this to obtain\nthe cotangent complex of a morphism of ringed topoi, a morphism of\nringed spaces, a morphism of schemes, a morphism of algebraic space, etc.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a site and let <MATH_0002> denote the\nassociated topos. Let <MATH_0003> denote a sheaf of rings\non <MATH_0004>. Let <MATH_0005> be the category of\n<MATH_0006>-algebras. Consider the pair of adjoint functors <MATH_0007> where\n<MATH_0008> is the forgetful functor and\n<MATH_0009> assigns to a sheaf of sets\n<MATH_0010> the polynomial algebra <MATH_0011> on\n<MATH_0012> over <MATH_0013>.\nLet <MATH_0014> be the simplicial object of\n<MATH_0015>\nconstructed in\nSimplicial, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nNow assume that <MATH_0016> is a homomorphism of sheaves\nof rings. Then <MATH_0017> is an object of the category\n<MATH_0018>. Denote\n<MATH_0019> the resulting\nsimplicial <MATH_0020>-algebra.\nRecall that\n<MATH_0021>,\n<MATH_0022>, and so on.\nRecall also that there is an augmentation\n<MATH_0023>\nwhere we view <MATH_0024> as a constant simplicial <MATH_0025>-algebra.\n\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:61da07139fd7de3374e0da5522fab25dc022c486c115400c9a042e7b5f58a92a",
      "unit_id": "tag:08UQ:prose-0001"
    },
